   "file": "content/FMA_32672/tier1.auto.md",
   "text": "Any short, irregular bone that is embedded in a tendon, and which functions to alter the direction of muscle pull, diminish friction, and modify pressure; sesamoid bones are found in various locations in the body, the largest of which is the patella.",
